      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not exactly - \"given that none of it is (CPU) architecture-specific\" - accesing it is archetecture specific, not event teling about interrupt handling.\nIn this particular case it is discusion about x86 IO/PORTS vs arm MMIO.\n\nCurent code have many asumptions about how UART and other divices working. Especialy in case of mapping/unmaping its memory and interrupt handling.\n\nIMHO: Static IO ports numbers should be mapped as rust enum.",
      "parentUuid": "ab2a3f54_c26f2275",
      "revId": "bac00e590d1671543b1b39b5cc8a24b1a6d4077c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
